      "side": 1,
      "message": "Sorry for not including the above comment in with Tom\u0027s, I didn\u0027t see it when I made the above comment (I think it came in while I was reviewing). It might be worth having a separate discussion on this. Is there a reason that this has to be stored as an array rather than a structure? On possible design is to define a structure that is bit compatible with the existing RO data buffer. Then devices with additional data(reset flags2, panic reason, etc) could wrap the RO data in a secondary structure that could be defined for each device type. This could be cleaner and much less error prone.",
      "parentUuid": "b9eaff2b_2c8cb818",
