      "writtenOn": "2022-02-23T18:36:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think we should try to do it for this CL, but what do you think about assigning explicit enum values to all the items? For example, if we ever changed one of the configs (`CONFIG_USB_PD_DUAL_ROLE`) after releasing RO, we\u0027d hit the same issue (unlikely with that specific config, but more could be added.). If they had explicit values it would be fine:\n\n```\nenum bkpdata_index {\n\tBKPDATA_INDEX_SCRATCHPAD \u003d 0,\t     \n\tBKPDATA_INDEX_SAVED_RESET_FLAGS \u003d 1,    \n#ifdef CONFIG_STM32_EXTENDED_RESET_FLAGS\n\tBKPDATA_INDEX_SAVED_RESET_FLAGS_2 \u003d 2,   \n#endif\n...\n```\n\nActually, I\u0027m not sure we could come up with a way to preserve compatibility with existing ROs easily with that. We could create separate versions for the RO/RW compatibility that we know about, but it\u0027s hard to know what variations other ECs might have used.",
